\par\par \b \uc2 RBA Says No Outright  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  In 2005/06  \b0\par\par\uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2006\par 04:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ian Macfarlane said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased earnings to A$1.16 billion in the financial year ending June 30, 2006, from A$997 million in the previous 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 Writing in the RBA's annual report tabled in federal parliament, Macfarlane said the increase in earnings was due to a rise in short-term interest rates in Australia, Europe and the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in earnings allowed the RBA to pay the federal government a A$1.48 billion dividend in the current financial year, the largest such payment since 2002/03.  \par \par \uc2 This year's dividend payment includes A$300 million deferred from the previous financial year.  \par \par \uc2 Macfarlane, who retires at the end of this week after a 10-year stint as governor, said the RBA's activities in 2005/06 took place against a backdrop of a strong global economy, where central banks around the world were gradually moving interest rates up to more normal levels.  \par \par \uc2 "Although world inflation is still relatively low, it has been increasing, as have yields on marketable securities," Macfarlane said in the foreword to the annual report. [ 12-09-06 0307GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 While there was an increase in underlying earnings, the RBA reported that realized gains amounted to just A$21 million in 2005/06, down from A$366 million in the previous year.  \par \par \uc2 Gains of A$362 million were realized from the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, losses of A$332 million were realized on holdings of foreign securities and there were losses of A$30 million on domestic assets, the RBA annual report revealed.  \par \par \uc2 "The loss on foreign investments reflected turnover in these assets, in the course of managing international reserves, at higher market yields than those at which they were purchased," the report said.  \par \par \uc2 "Gains of A$21 million were realized from the sale of gold coin that the Reserve Bank decided it no longer needed to hold."  \par \par \uc2 Macfarlane confirmed there were no outright \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertaken by the RBA during 2005/06.  \par \par \uc2 "With the Australian dollar moving in a relatively narrow range during the year, at a level a little above its long-run average, the Reserve Bank saw no need to try to influence the exchange rate," the annual report said.  \par \par \uc2 The RBA hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since 2001, the report added.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did replenish its foreign reserves by a further A$2.3 billion during the year, although the scale of the replenishment was scaled back from previous years.  \par \par \uc2 Macfarlane also pointed to the growing task involved in managing the RBA's assets.  \par \par \uc2 "Management of the Reserve Bank's balance sheet has become a larger job as its size has grown: total assets now exceed A$100 billion, compared with A$58 billion five years ago," Macfarlane said.  \par \par \uc2 The RBA also maintains asset revaluation reserves, the balances of which reflect the amount by which the market value of its holdings of gold and property exceed the prices at which they were purchased, the report said.  \par \par \uc2 At June 30, 2006, balances in these reserves totaled A$2.35 billion, A$672 million higher than a year earlier, mainly reflecting the increase in the price of gold, it said.  \par \par \uc2 The RBA holds about 80 metric tons of gold valued about A$2.2 billion at the end of June. In past years, this gold has been on loan to gold dealers on a fully collateralized basis but due to falling demand, only 53 tons were on loan at the end of June 2006.  \par \par \uc2 Over the course of 2005/06, the RBA's holdings of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  under swaps increase to A$34 billion from A$30 billion in the previous financial year.  \par \par \uc2 The RBA's annual report was posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website ahead of its formal presentation to parliament, expected later Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Although formally independent, the RBA still reports to the parliament through semiannual testimony by the governor and the presentation of an annual report.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Owen Brown, Dow Jones Newswires; 612 8235 2964; owen.brown@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Graham Morgan \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-09-06 0334GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060912e29c0002n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
