\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie recovery scuttled by yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk.  \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 00:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, March 18 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar was again trying to re-establish itself above 74 U.S. cents on Thursday after dipping briefly offshore as the yen gained against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , notably the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The Aussie has a high correlation with the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which appeared to bear the resulting brunt of speculation that Japan may have ended its heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro/yen cross fell to a six-week low overnight.  \par \par \uc2 Such talk re-surfaced after Japan's influential former top finance official Eisuke Sakakibara told Reuters Japan would have to end its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point.  \par \par \uc2 However, National \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank strategist Peter Jolly is sceptical that Japan was ready to stop.  \par \par \uc2 "We continue to believe that the Japanese authorities will continue to smooth the JPY's appreciation," Jolly said.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:00 a.m. (2300 GMT) Aussie/yen was 80.06/16 yen compared with 80.63/73 yen late here on Wednesday after hitting a low for 2004 of 79.65 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Versus the U.S. dollar the AUD was $0.7403/08 compared with $0.7427/32 late here on Wednesday and after an offshore low of $0.7364. However, it remains well well above last week's low for the year of around $0.7250.  \par \par \uc2 The Aussie had firmed on Wednesday after comments by the Federal Reserve suggested the United States will retain a low interest rate regime for a while yet by acknowledging the lagging employment recovery.  \par \par \uc2 While local interest rate markets are also of the view that the Reserve Bank may have completed its tightening cycle for now after a run of soft data, it will still carry a 425 basis point interest rate premium over the United States.  \par \par \uc2 However, the Aussie has failed to make a dent in resistance around the 74.35/40 cent mark in recent days.  \par \par \uc2 "The AUD will need to get itself above the $0.7435/40 region to take on $0.7490. A break of the latter will signal a break of the daily declining downtrend from the mid February peak (of $0.8005), thus opening bluer skies and a potential test of 0.7645," said NAB's Jolly.  \par \par \uc2 "On the downside, support is at $0.7250/60, which looks robust," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of Australia releases its monthly bulletin at 3:00 p.m. (0400 GMT). The report will show to what degree the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the Aussie in February as it continues to replenish its reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h0036v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
