\par\par \b \uc2 NZ,  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  Should Unite On Any  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  - HSBC  \b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the New Zealand and Australian central banks to drive their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down should be coordinated, according to a top economist.  \par \par \uc2 Investment bank HSBC's (HBC) chief economist in Australia, John Edwards, said in a research note Monday that New Zealand and Australia are small players on the world stage and could add to their firepower, authority and credibility by acting jointly.  \par \par \uc2 The recent appreciation of the U.S. dollar, which has given the Australian and New Zealand economies some respite from the continued strengthening of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , means \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to be carried out "anytime soon" but it can't be ruled out if U.S. dollar depreciation resumes in a big way, Edwards said.  \par \par \uc2 The Australian and New Zealand dollars are "very highly correlated" and "it would be ridiculous for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to act alone. If the Reserve Bank of Australia and the Reserve Bank of New Zealand are not already talking about this possibility, they certainly should be," Edwards said.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand's current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve target is a range of 1.4 billion to 1.7 billion special drawing rights, a notional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the International Monetary Fund. Actual reserves stand around 1.5 billion SDRs, which equates to NZ$3.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are about A$35 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The potential for New Zealand to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since the New Zealand dollar was floated in March 1985 has weighed on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen, in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires Feb. 19, gave his clearest hint yet that he is prepared to break with convention.  \par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't rest easy on the assumption that the settings for the last 20 years are going to remain unchanged," Cullen said in the interview. "I would be inclined to factor that into one's judgment."  \par \par \uc2 Edwards said that if the U.S. dollar resumed depreciating and the Australian dollar broke through US$0.81 and kept rising - it is currently around US$0.7750 - then the "timing and nature" of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would become the central issue.  \par \par \uc2 The same would apply if the New Zealand dollar, currently around US$0.6880, again broke through US$0.70 and kept on appreciating, he said. In February, the New Zealand dollar hit a seven-year high of US$0.7102.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be successful in limited circumstances, Edwards said.  \par \par \uc2 "There needs to be a widely shared sense that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indeed overshot...the market conditions also need to be right. The perfect circumstance for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is when the market is very long and traders are overextended," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "In this circumstance, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can cause a great deal of injury to long positions in Australia and New Zealand dollars at relatively little cost."  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Dawn Lye [ 01-03-04 0053GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040301e03100018\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
