\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie dlr finding base after huge 80c rejection.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Colin Brinsden  \par \uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2004\par 00:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar was finding a base around the 79 U.S. cent mark on Thursday after a massive rejection of 80 cents overnight in tandem with a one percent drop in the euro from a record high against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Aussie matched its March 1997 high of 80.05 cents in European trading as the euro struck a new peak of $1.2927, but this proved the trigger for profit-taking as investors became anxious over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem gains in the euro and yen.  \par \par \uc2 The USD also made sharp gains against the Canadian dollar, yen and sterling in a broad rally.  \par \par \uc2 "The USD is finding especially good support against the yen and the euro towards 105 yen and $1.2900/$1.300 respectively. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a factor in both these levels," said National \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank strategist Michael Jansen.  \par \par \uc2 For the AUD, Jansen said with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  already stretched on a number of the crosses it cannot rally on its own accord unless the yen and euro rally.  \par \par \uc2 At 10:00 a.m. (2300 GMT) the AUD was $0.7898/7903 compared with $0.7972/77 late here on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term the Aussie could struggle, and the retracement will deepen on a breakdown through $0.7860. It made a low of $0.7874 overnight.  \par \par \uc2 BEARISH ENGULFING PATTERN  \par \par \uc2 "The AUD has currently posted one of the most virulent technical signals around - the bearish engulfing pattern - formed when the market trades a new high relative to the previous day but also trades a new low and closes towards the day's low," said NAB's Jansen.  \par \par \uc2 However, Jansen said the buying at the low was reasonably robust and the underlying fundamentals remain solid.  \par \par \uc2 At the high the Aussie had rallied seven percent this year on top of the huge 34 percent advance over 2003, buoyed by a two-year downtrend in the USD, its high yielding status and from the global economic recovery as a commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Aussie has an interest rate premium of 425 basis points over the United States, which could grow in coming months with recent commentary by the Reserve Bank doing little to quell speculation of another tightening in the 5.25 percent cash rate.  \par \par \uc2 The Aussie gains over the past year came despite a steady flow of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling, largely on behalf of the Government, but more so for its own account in recent months as it replenishes its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The market will get an update on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's January AUD sales when it releases its Bulletin at 3:00 p.m. (0400 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 Other than selling to build up reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not appeared overly perturbed by the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its recent statements.  \par \par \uc2 This is in contrast with central banks in Europe and Japan, where the latter has openly sold to stem the yen rise, while the former has so far stuck to verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as far as the market can tell.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040218e02i004nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
