\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie dlr push higher runs out of steam, for now.  \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2004\par 06:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Miranda Maxwell\par     SYDNEY, Feb 18 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar\par shied away from 80 U.S. cents on Wednesday with traders saying\par option-related selling held the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back after its push to\par seven-year highs overnight.\par  \par     Still, many strategists were confident it was now only\par matter of time until the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pierces the 80 cent level.\par     "The scenario for the Australian dollar is one where it is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  likely to keep rising, with a move to 82 cents or more on the   \par \par \uc2  cards for the next few months," said Stephen Koukoulas, chief   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Chart resistance stands at the March 1997 high of 80.05\par followed by the December 1996 high of 82.15.\par     At 4 p.m. (0500 GMT), the Aussie was trading at $0.7972/77,\par compared with $0.7933/38 late on Tuesday and $0.7988 overnight,\par the highest since March 1997.\par     The Aussie rose broadly against a range of rivals such as\par the euro, yen, Canadian and Singapore dollars.\par     Helping the Aussie was a rally in metal prices, seeing\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par COMEX copper reach levels unseen since May 1996 and gold rise\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.4 percent. On the charts, the 10-day moving average moved up\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above its 20-day counterpart in recent days, forming a bullish\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cross.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is hard to sees what stalls the momentum. A break of 80\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cents now appears inevitable," said Geoff Bowmer, divisional\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Macquarie Bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Markets believe the U.S. dollar correction has further to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par go. Very near-term, though, there are likely to be sellers\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of 80 cents," he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With Australia's interest rates at 5.25 percent, investors\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are reaping around four to five percent more in yield than\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offered by the greenback or Japanese yen. And unlike the Bank\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Japan, the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not have a pattern\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of large \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the rise in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the door open for\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a third rate increase, saying strong demand for credit showed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent policy has been stimulatory and prices of assets such as\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par property could not be ignored.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The RBA remains one of the few major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not complained about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation thus far," said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ashley Davies, strategist at UBS.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, Davies said with the market already long Aussie,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to be at 78 U.S. cents in a month and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 79 in three months.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In local data, the annualised growth rate of the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Westpac-Melbourne Institute leading index of economic activity,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which normally indicates the likely pace of economic activity\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par six to nine months in the future, rose 1.7 points to 3.5\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in December, above its long-term trend of 3.3 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040218e02i000vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
