\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  RBA Bought Net A$1.1B In  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  01-02 \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2002\par 02:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CANBERRA -(Dow Jones)- The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the year ended June 30, 2002, amounted to net purchases of A$1.1 billion. \par \par \uc2  "During 2001-02, the only significant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred just after Sept. 11, and was motivated mainly by the Reserve Bank's concerns about the extreme uncertainty in markets generally at the time," the Reserve Bank said in its annual report. \par \par \uc2  Through the rest of the year, the Reserve Bank didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market because the exchange rate, even though it remained low by comparison with its longer-run average level, tended to be either relatively stable or rising, the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank said it also sold A$5.3 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the federal government in 2001-02. \par \par \uc2  Early in the year these sales were met partly from reserve assets and partly from interest earnings on foreign investments and other transactions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "For the year as a whole, net purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from all sources, plus interest earnings on reserves, were slightly larger than sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the government, so overall transactions added to net reserves," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  Part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold to the government during the year was for repayments of some of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps that the government had previously entered into, the Reserve Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The repayments were part of a program agreed between the Reserve Bank and the government following a review of Australia's swap arrangements, which concluded that all of Australia's outstanding foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps should be gradually run off, the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The review was conducted after the government recorded large unrealized losses on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps portfolio. The losses amounted to A$1.92 billion in 2000-01 after losses of A$1.11 billion in 1999-00. \par \par \uc2  -By Rebecca Thurlow, Dow Jones Newswires; \par \par \uc2  61-2-6208-0902; rebecca.thurlow@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020828dy8s0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
