\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie dollar stalls as M&A inflow hopes fade. \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2001\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar was steady against the greenback on Thursday as dealers pondered an uncertain global growth outlook and waited to see if anticipated M&A inflows would materialise. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie leapt two percent on Monday, touching one-month highs on speculation that Australian miner WMC Ltd was about to be snapped up by U.S. aluminium giant Alcoa . \par \par \uc2  But with no firm bid yet on the table, the Aussie has fallen steadily since then, drfiting to lows around US$0.5070 in Asian trade before stabilising in Europe. By 1035 GMT, the Aussie was trading at US$0.5082 , little changed from the New York close. \par \par \uc2  "The Aussie's surge early this week was linked to M&A rumours, but now there is considerable uncertainty," said Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  "As a small, open economy, Australia is also vulnerable to the slowdown in global demand, which is likely to cap rallies in the near term." \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to data showing the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in September to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as risk aversion intensified after the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed it bought a net A$778 million of Aussie dollars on the spot market, its largest monthly purchase since November last year when it bought A$860 million. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar has tracked the Aussie's moves this week and was trading at US$0.4165 . The Canadian dollar was mired near earlier two-week lows around C$1.5730 as markets awaited inflation and manufacturing data later in the session. \par \par \uc2  "The Canadian dollar is looking weak from a chart perspective and selling has been technically-driven," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  M&A activity aside, analysts said there was little positive momentum for dollar-bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the global economy weak and continued anthrax scares in the United States and elsewhere likely to knock already fragile consumer and market confidence. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dxai04kii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
