\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie dollar sits precariously above US$0.50 mark. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 12 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar hovered precariously above three-month lows in Europe on Thursday, after wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented a break of the key US$0.50 level. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie fell within a whisker of the psychological chart barrier in Asia as risk aversion prompted an exodus into safer, more liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it bounced half a cent from its lows as talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  swept trading floors. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. The bank regularly stepped into the market between September last year and April to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Rumours the RBA were sniffing around has lifted the Aussie dollar off its lows," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. "There has been no confirmation of this, but the market knows that the RBA is not afraid to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar stood at US$0.5045 at 1000 GMT. Its bounce from lows around US$0.5010 also lifted the New Zealand dollar from one-week troughs around US$0.4025 . The Canadian dollar stood at C$1.5275 , within sight of Wednesday's two-week lows. \par \par \uc2  Peripheral \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been hit hard in recent days as escalating emerging market concerns have fuelled capital flight from more illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Risk premiums on emerging market debt rose on Wednesday to their highest since September 1998 in the wake of Russia's debt default, according to J.P. Morgan's Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus. \par \par \uc2  "Emerging market concerns are feeding through to the Aussie which is still sitting precariously in my view," said a trader at an Australian bank in London. \par \par \uc2  He added that the Australian dollar's break through several chart support levels had left it looking vulnerable on a technical basis. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00hg0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
