\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie dlr jittery, haunted by sub-50 cent risk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Colin Brinsden \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 08:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, July 12 (Reuters) - Having thought that a sub-50 U.S. cent Australian dollar was well and truly history just a few weeks ago, analysts now see a distinct risk of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wearing a "four" big figure before long. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie took a big hit early in Thursday's local session, dropping to a three-month low of around 50.10 cents on stop-loss selling as it got caught up in emerging market risk hysteria, and was only saved by rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the talk when approached by Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "It's now a game of cat and mouse in terms of market rumours about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Robert Rennie, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac. \par \par \uc2  "Certainly psychologically I think if we were to break down through 50, you would start to see additional weakness coming through," Rennie said. \par \par \uc2  At 4:07 p.m. (0607 GMT) the AUD was $0.5048/53 compared with $0.5100/05 late here on Wednesday and after a high of 51.30 earlier in the weak. \par \par \uc2  Initial support on the Aussie below 50 cents is 49.80. \par \par \uc2  On its trade weighted index the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a four and a half week low of 49.5 after 50.0 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  AUD UNDERVALUED \par \par \uc2  In a speech earlier this week RBA Governor Ian Macfarlane gave an upbeat appraisal of the local economy, but felt the local dollar was still undervalued and that there were still risks to Australia from global weakness. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had regularly stepped into the market between September last year and April to prop up the Aussie, or to at least smooth flows in the market, buying a total of some 2.51 billion of AUD. \par \par \uc2  However, in the last RBA bulletin it showed zero buying in net terms during May, although during that period the Aussie had extended its rally from the April 2 record low of 47.75 cents to a May high of 53.20 cents. \par \par \uc2  Since then a sustained break of 53 cents has been elusive, and despite a steady stream of positive domestic data, the Aussie has repeatedly failed to sustain rallies. \par \par \uc2  And those missed opportunities to extend the Aussie's recovery had now left it vulnerable with markets becoming increasingly agitated by risks in emerging markets, either be it Argentina, Turkey or neighbouring Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This normally spells bad news for a liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Aussie, whether as a proxy for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or being a peripheral dollar bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors draw in their risk taking horns. \par \par \uc2  "An escalation of problems in either Argentina or Turkey would prompt further safe haven flows to the U.S. dollar, with the likely result being a sub 50 cents Aussie dollar," said Craig James, chief economist at Commonwealth Securities. \par \par \uc2  As such, and as the market pondered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and offshore developments, Thursday's labour force data for June drew little sustained attention, although talk of another round of RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  circulated the market shortly after the report's release. \par \par \uc2  Overall employment fell 3,000, much in line with median expectations for a flat outcome, although full-time employment dropped 39,400. Unemployment stayed at 6.9 percent as expected. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00d4g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
