\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Hits Another Record Low In NY Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 20:25\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The Australian dollar hit another record low at $0.4937 in New York trading Wednesday, the latest in a series of all-time bottoms against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  At 2:25 p.m. EST (1925 GMT), the Australian dollar was buying 0.4953 U.S. dollars, down from US$0.5024 earlier in Sydney and US$0.5079 late Tuesday in Sydney. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Australian dollar hit $0.5005 earlier in London trading, a trader said, but had not entered at the current lows, given "one-way flow" and "very illiquid" overseas trading. \par \par \uc2  Another trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been rumored to be in the market during Tuesday trading, but that the RBA's role in bolstering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unconfirmed. The RBA's forays would not be enough to stave off the Australian dollar's slide, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Generally the nature of their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to smooth the course downward, rather than to create a turnaround," he said. \par \par \uc2  Australia reported Wednesday a 15.4% fall in consumer sentiment in March, adding to a list of mounting pressures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last week's announcement that the Australian economy had suffered its first contraction in nine and a half years. \par \par \uc2  -by Jennifer Downey, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2019; jennifer.downey@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010710dx3e00kzr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\