\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: Australia RBA Worried About A$, Lies Low So Far \b0\par\par\uc2  By Iain McDonald \par \uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 05:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANBERRA -(Dow Jones)- The Reserve Bank of Australia is likely very\par concerned about the economic effects of a further sharp depreciation in\par the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  So far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept a low profile in the still orderly Australian dollar market but public and concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't be ruled out if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls much further. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar's fall to a record low of US$0.5061 in New York and London trading Thursday appears to have been orderly so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't need to step in and reestablish a professional market place. \par \par \uc2  And the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weaker levels will help exports, as Treasurer Peter Costello pointed out in a radio interview Friday. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen 23% since peaking at US$0.6685 in January 2000 - a drop quite large enough to boost exports and help local producers compete against imports. \par \par \uc2  The country's current account deficit has halved in 18 months. \par \par \uc2  Further falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could significantly hurt confidence, damaging an already weak economy. \par \par \uc2  A renewed Australian dollar slump would also ignite imported inflation, which mightn't flow through to retail prices because of competitive pressures but could squeeze corporate margins. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank would be very reluctant to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply improve from here but equally there are no economic gains and considerable economic risks from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deteriorating from here," says HSBC Markets chief economist John Edwards. \par \par \uc2  "There are risks to inflation and at a certain point,...there has to be risks to confidence (and) the willingness of foreign investors to hold Australian dollars," he says. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      AUD/USD Bounces From US$0.5061 Low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For now, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears willing to hold off from concerted\par and public \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When the unit touched its low in New York and London, it bounced\par strongly, encouraging speculation that the Reserve Bank had supported\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But most market participants are skeptical that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was involved, instead attributing the bounce to buying by\par large U.S. names.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has recovered to as high as US$0.5130 during local\par trading Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think they were in," says a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer at a local\par bank who doesn't want to be named.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think you can say the market hasn't been a professional\par market," he says. "Trading has been controlled."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Moves have been a bit whippy but at no stage have spreads blown out,"\par he adds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the past, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to restore order to the\par market when buyers have disappeared and traders have been stacked on the\par sell side.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the Reserve Bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past year haven't been on\par the same scale as in 1998 when hedge funds sold the Australian dollar in\par massive amounts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At that time, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent A$3.87 billion over five months\par to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from sliding.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the five months between September last year and January this year,\par the Reserve Bank has bought just A$1.67 billion in its market\par transactions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Foreign Portfolio Investment In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Slow\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts say the lack of Reserve Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflects a\par realistic view by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that perceptions have altered on the\par Australian economy's ability to ride out a global slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The catalyst for weaker sentiment toward the economy's prospects came\par Wednesday when the country's national accounts showed gross domestic\par product contracted 0.6% in the fourth quarter from the third quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Reserve Bank has become a lot more realistic about the prospects\par for the economy," says Westpac Banking Corp.'s \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist,\par Robert Rennie. "And that may extend to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't be ruled out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If you look at (the Reserve Bank's monthly figures) over the past\par five months they have been active in each of those five months," says\par another strategist who didn't want to be named. "It is quite possible\par that they have continued to have done what they have done over the past\par five months."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Behind the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall is a lack of foreign interest in Australian\par equity and fixed-income assets to offset the country's current account\par deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors are still seeking assets directly through takeovers\par but foreign buying of Australian bonds and equity portfolio investment\par has been slow.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Also unsettling foreign investors is a possibility that the government\par could block or place conditions on Royal Dutch/Shell's A$10 billion bid\par for Australia's Woodside Petroleum Ltd. (A.WPL).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Treasurer Peter Costello has until April 24 to decide on whether to\par approve the bid and Prime Minister John Howard has already said a number\par of times he understands concerns about the level of foreign ownership in\par Australia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As long as offshore investment into Australian industry is unsettled\par offshore would view investment in Australia as a potentially higher-risk\par option," Westpac's Rennie says.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Iain McDonald, Dow Jones Newswires; 61-2-6208-0901;\par iain.mcdonald@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx39010v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
