\par\par \b \uc2  A$ bounces back from record lows vs US$ in Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2000\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 22 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar bounced back from this week's record lows against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, buoyed by talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support in the options market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a substantial buyer of short-dated Aussie call options caught \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders on the hop, triggering stop-loss orders above US$0.5180. \par \par \uc2  The identity of the buyer was unknown, but talk centred on the Reserve Bank of Australia, which has said before it has used options as a means of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was a big buyer of short-dated options with strikes at US$0.5150 and this was rumoured to be the Reserve Bank," said Andrew Baxter, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Commonwealth Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The RBA has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  fairly successfully in the options market in the past, and this move caught short-term players on the back foot." \par \par \uc2  The options purchase took place when the Australian dollar was trading just above US$0.51 in the spot market, traders said. The Aussie pushed as high as US$0.52 in early European trade, gaining over a cent from its record low of US$0.5070 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar has fallen over 20 percent against the U.S. dollar since the start of the year amid signs of slowing global growth, falls in commodity prices and regional Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness. \par \par \uc2  "The Aussie looks well supported at these levels, although we have seen some selling interest from U.S. banks close to the $0.52 level which will cap upside," said a London-based trader. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar rose in sympathy with the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising as high as US$0.3990 , almost a cent above Wednesday's low. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar also pushed sharply higher on Wednesday, hitting one-week peaks around C$1.5480 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Canadian September retail trade data and employment insurance data are due for release at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbm015n6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
