\par\par \b \uc2  Australian dollar eyes record lows in Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2000\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar fell to within half a cent of record lows against the U.S. dollar in Europe on Monday, amid waning expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its support. \par \par \uc2  The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the main counter-balance to investors selling the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts and traders said, due to the relative appeal of the U.S. dollar. U.S. interest rates are higher than Australian interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Buy orders were placed at around US$0.5180 during Sydney trade amid talk of Australian dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sydney and London-based traders said. \par \par \uc2  But these buy orders disappeared in European trade, London traders added, allowing the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall to around US$0.5150 , its weakest since record lows around US$0.5110 set on October 31, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  "This is all flow-driven - there is no domestic news," said Michael Derks, international strategist at Commonwealth Bank of Australia in London. \par \par \uc2  "We will try and retest the all-time low over the next 24 hours," he added. \par \par \uc2  The RBA confirmed last week it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several recent occasions to support the Australian dollar, heightening wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Aussie dollar has been getting easier all week," said a London-based trader. "There was a lot of talk in Sydney of bids by the RBA at US$0.5180, though we didn't see them." \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar was trading at its lowest since Thursday around US$0.3975 , two percent above record lows around US$0.39 set on October 18. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar, meanwhile, traded within half a cent of its lowest levels in more than two years set on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market focus was on the weakness of Canadian stocks and the outcome of the U.S. presidential election. A victory for Republican George W. Bush is seen resulting in higher U.S. interest rates, with a knock-on negative impact for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at the day's low of C$1.5588 per dollar , from Friday's low of C$1.5625. \par \par \uc2  Canadian wholesale trade data for September are due at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbk019bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
