\par\par \b \uc2  A$ kept afloat amid RBA wariness in Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2000\par 13:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar held ground above recent two-week lows against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, propped by speculation about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In its semi-annual statement on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a number of occasions in recent weeks to support the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market saw a rally in the Australian unit on Wednesday as evidence that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, heightening speculation about further action. \par \par \uc2  "There is still a chance the RBA might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again and this is keeping the Australian dollar supported," said a dealer at an Australian bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "On the downside people are focussing on $US0.5170/80." \par \par \uc2  At 1155 GMT the Australian dollar was hovering around US$0.52 , up from two-week lows around US$0.5175 it hit on Wednesday but still within a cent of record lows around US$0.5110 reached on October 31. \par \par \uc2  "There's good reason to believe that the RBA will continue to intermittently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Richard Franulovich, economist at Westpac in London \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to get too bearish on the Australian dollar and I wouldn't be going overly short on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being." \par \par \uc2  Official figures on Thursday revised the rise in average weekly ordinary time earnings for the three months to August up to 1.9 percent from 1.7 percent in an initial estimate and 1.2 percent in the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  But the market impact was muted as analysts said the survey is often distorted by other factors. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the New Zealand dollar was holding ground near one-week highs just above $0.40 hit earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was struggling around $1.5525 against the U.S. dollar, only a flicker away from 23-month lows beyond C$1.5530 it hit on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian composite index for October is due at 1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbg01ugw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
