\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie stuck below $0.52, ignores supportive talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2000\par 22:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2  AU$S/Term range *Support *Restance *RSI-14 *MA-10  *MA-20 \par \par \uc2    *0.5150/5265  *0.5165  *0.5220   *37.82  *0.5237 *0.5233 \par \par \uc2  -------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - Nov 15 -------------- \par \par \uc2      *Offshore range roughly $0.5185/5221 \par \par \uc2      *Aussie dollar tests key support at 51.80 cents, the level \par \par \uc2  at which the Reserve Bank swooped in to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \par \par \uc2  November 2. Barrage of comments from policymakers in recent \par \par \uc2  days no help. \par \par \uc2      *Treasurer Costello says recent Aussie link to euro is \par \par \uc2  illogical, dollar will eventually reflect fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      *Mid-year budget review due at midday, budget surplus \par \par \uc2  expected to be revised up. \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Nov 15 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar remained trapped in a tight range around 52 U.S. cents overnight but with a bias towards the downside, once again paying no heed to supportive comments from policymakers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar spent most of the New York session testing support at 51.8 U.S. cents, the level at which the Reserve Bank swooped in to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on November 2. \par \par \uc2  By 8:10 a.m. (2110 GMT), the Australian dollar had retreated to $0.5190/95 from $0.5214/19 here late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Treasurer Peter Costello added his thoughts to those of the Prime Minister and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days that the dollar would eventually recover to reflect fundamentals, comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again duly ignored. \par \par \uc2  Noting there was no logic to the Aussie's recent link with the euro, Costello said: "I think there will be a reassessment and in the long term the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reflect the fundamentals." \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank said on Monday the dollar had appeared to stabilise, and last week Governor Ian Macfarlane said it was below fair value. \par \par \uc2  But logic has failed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  all year, as it declined more than 20 percent despite solid economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's inability to capitalise on a vulnerable U.S. dollar and a continued lack of demand are once again ominous signs," said National Australia Bank strategist Greg McKenna. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar firmed overnight but remains uncertain while the outcome of the U.S. presidential election remains disputed. Overnight a Florida state judge upheld an evening deadline to end vote-counting from last week's poll. \par \par \uc2  McKenna said the price action in the Aussie suggested that investors remain wary of the assets of both \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe, but are equally cautious of any further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Fresh evidence of the nation's solid fundamentals is expected on Wednesday when the government revises up its budget surplus forecast for 2000/01 in the mid-year review. \par \par \uc2  The review at midday (0100 GMT) could also revise up growth forecasts to 4.0 percent from 3.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Westpac consumer sentiment survey for November is due at 11 a.m. (0000 GMT). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbe021mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
