\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up In Late Trade; Watching A$, Euro Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2000\par 06:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The New Zealand dollar was higher versus the U.S. dollar in afternoon trade Friday, finishing the local session well bid on the back of a stronger Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the New Zealand and Australian dollars will continue to watch the euro for guidance following the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  They noted the euro's move against the U.S. dollar is also a barometer for the uncertain U.S. presidential election outcome. \par \par \uc2  Around 0430 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.4000, up from US$0.3963 late Thursday in Wellington and higher than its local open at US$0.3989. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded very quietly in a range of between US$0.3987 and US$0.4008 Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer said the New Zealand dollar has been well bid Friday, with solid buying by a local investor taking it to the session peak. \par \par \uc2  "But all in all it's been dead - as it has been all week," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer picked a US$0.3960 to US$0.4010 range overnight. \par \par \uc2  "Outside of that, the broad topside is US$0.4054 - the previous (Oct. 30) high, which is what we need to get through to get confirmation of a bull rally," he said. \par \par \uc2  "On the downside we look for support anywhere in the US$0.3900/50 window," he added. \par \par \uc2  "There's no local drivers - the aussie is still supported by (fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by) the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the (U.S.) election and ECB activity," he added. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar is quoted at A$0.7590, up from A$0.7574 late Thursday and higher than A$0.7551 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar was quoted at Y43.07, up from Y42.52 late Thursday and higher than Y42.81 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar is 46.72, up from 46.46 late Thursday and higher than 46.51 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0330 GMT, the Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions Index, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted index measure of the New Zealand dollar and yields on 90-day bank bills, was at minus-1037. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Wood, Dow Jones Newswires; 64 4 801 8960; alan.wood@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwba05elk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
