\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie dlr scoots to 53c after euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2000\par 22:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2  AU$S/Term range *Support *Restance *RSI-14 *MA-10  *MA-20 \par \par \uc2    *0.5200/5340  *0.5240  *0.5285   *53.51  *0.5227 *0.5251 \par \par \uc2  -------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - Nov 6 ---------------- \par \par \uc2      *Offshore range roughly $0.5230/5305 \par \par \uc2      *Australian dollar gets a lift from the euro, which gained \par \par \uc2  fresh support on another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *But euro gains were limited by realisation that ECB was on \par \par \uc2  its own in buying euros, in contrast to coordinated G7 support \par \par \uc2  six weeks ago. \par \par \uc2      *Aussie also boosted by rumours of modest RBA buying \par \par \uc2  through Friday night, on alert for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *RBA board meets on Tuesday and no rate change expected. \par \par \uc2      SYDNEY, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar made \par \par \uc2  further progress away from last week's record low in overnight \par \par \uc2  trade, getting a much-needed lift from the euro which rose on \par \par \uc2  another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2   But the euro's gains were pared as the market realised the \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on its own in buying the impoverished \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in contrast to the coordinated G7 support that \par \par \uc2  surprised markets six weeks ago. \par \par \uc2      Rumours of continued modest Reserve Bank buying of Aussie \par \par \uc2  dollars through the offshore session on Friday helped the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breach resistance around $0.5280, although it has \par \par \uc2  slipped back to that level by early Monday trade. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was now awaiting the outcome of the Reserve Bank \par \par \uc2  board meeting on Tuesday, which is expected to hold rates \par \par \uc2  steady. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By 8:20 a.m.\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at $0.5277/82, after earlier rising more than half a cent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its $0.5232/37 level here late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Bank strategist Greg McKenna said the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the euro and reputed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the Aussie\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signalled that both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were no longer one-way bets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But he said upside progress would continue to be tough.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Aussie holding above the $0.5200/25 region will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par embolden bulls, but the price action continues to tell us the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market still sees AUD in a downward trend and thus we see\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength as a selling opportunity," McKenna said in a morning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par note. The Reserve Bank holds its policy-setting board meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Tuesday, but analysts polled by Reuters saw only a 30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent chance of a rate rise afterwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Any announcement would come on Wednesday morning at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RBA's usual money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The only data on Monday is the ANZ Bank job advertisement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par series, which is expected to bounce back from Olympic doldrums\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It will give a guide to the outlook for the labour market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of Thursday's official labour force report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     RBA Governor Ian Macfarlane also makes a rare speech on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday evening in Melbourne. No topic has been given.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb502lu6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
