\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie plays bit part as G7 tries to beef up euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 00:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2  AU$S/Term range *Support *Restance *RSI-14 *MA-10  *MA-20 \par \par \uc2    *0.5400/5590  *0.5470  *0.5550   *35.03  *0.5480 *0.5585 \par \par \uc2  -------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - Sept 25-------------- \par \par \uc2      *Offshore range roughly $0.5588/5420 \par \par \uc2      *The Australian dollar proved a bit of a bystander as the \par \par \uc2  euro was whipped around by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, \par \par \uc2  and is still short of levels where it would convince the market \par \par \uc2  that a base has been formed. \par \par \uc2  *The Aussie jumped to a high near 56 U.S. cents on Friday \par \par \uc2  as G7 central banks took markets off-guard with coordinated \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro ahead of the G7 meeting in \par \par \uc2  Prague over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  *Market talk the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \par \par \uc2  the Aussie during Friday's mayhem. \par \par \uc2      SYDNEY, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar proved a \par \par \uc2  bit of a bystander as the euro was whipped around by \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, and is still well short of levels \par \par \uc2  where it would convince the market that a base has been formed. \par \par \uc2      The Aussie charged to near 56 U.S. cents at one stage late \par \par \uc2  on Friday -- over two cents above last week's all time low of \par \par \uc2  53.63 cents --  as G7 central banks took markets off-guard with \par \par \uc2  coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2      The Aussie subsequently retreated to around Friday's local \par \par \uc2  close, even though there was talk of the Reserve Bank having \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the markets were in disarray during the G7 \par \par \uc2  blitz. \par \par \uc2      At 8:30 a.m. (2130 GMT) the Aussie was at US$0.5476/81 \par \par \uc2  compared with US$0.5461/66 late here on Friday. \par \par \uc2      "The Aussie has been a bystander up until now. But I would \par \par \uc2  say the market would do well to hedge against against an upside \par \par \uc2  move," said Mark Adams, head of institutional sales at National \par \par \uc2  Australia Bank. \par \par \uc2      "We would really need to start breaking up over levels like \par \par \uc2  56.50 cents before we saw any change-around in the Aussie at \par \par \uc2  the moment," he added. \par \par \uc2      Heavy demand for U.S assets and a strong correlation with \par \par \uc2  the euro on charts has contributed to a near 20 percent decline \par \par \uc2  in the Aussie this year against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2      The concerted support for the euro took markets by surprise \par \par \uc2  as it not only came before this weekend's G7 meeting in Prague, \par \par \uc2  but also included the support of the Federal Reserve, which was \par \par \uc2  expected to sit pat until after the U.S. Presidential \par \par \uc2  elections. \par \par \uc2      The G7 communique was also more blunt than had been \par \par \uc2  expected, saying it would continue to monitor the market \par \par \uc2  closely and cooperate in action if necessary. \par \par \uc2      Richard Yetsenga, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank said \par \par \uc2  if this marks the end of the U.S. dollar's upward cycle then \par \par \uc2  buying the Aussie at current levels is likely to be a \par \par \uc2  profitable trade. \par \par \uc2      "However, the G7's actions do not increase the return on \par \par \uc2  Australian assets compared with the U.S.; volatility is likely \par \par \uc2  to remain high; and Friday's price action was not that \par \par \uc2  encouraging," Yetsenga said. \par \par \uc2      He expected a break of a 54.50/55.00 cent range would \par \par \uc2  determine the Aussie's next move. \par \par \uc2      Local data is again thin this week, and with the local \par \par \uc2  focus on the Olympics, the Aussie remains at the mercy of \par \par \uc2  offshore developments. \par \par \uc2      The August trade balance of goods and services, August \par \par \uc2  motor registrations and August private sector credit data are \par \par \uc2  due on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9o06ndi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
