\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie dlr hits new lows as euro, Asia woes weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 23:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2  AU$S/Term range *Support *Restance *RSI-14 *MA-10  *MA-20 \par \par \uc2    *0.5400/5550  *0.5400  *0.5450   *17.32  *0.5553 *0.5647 \par \par \uc2  -------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - Sept 19 -------------- \par \par \uc2      *Offshore range roughly $0.5407/5458 \par \par \uc2      *Aussie, kiwi sold to new record lows in tandem with euro \par \par \uc2      *RBA seen likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on any move below US$0.5400 \par \par \uc2      *New worries over Asia add to negative sentiment \par \par \uc2      *Oil/Wall St woes seen as precursor to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  turnaround \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar ploughed new \par \par \uc2  record lows on Tuesday just above key support at US$0.5400, \par \par \uc2  weighed down again by the euro and new concerns over Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers here saw no end in sight to the pressure on the \par \par \uc2  Aussie, with only the prospect of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) likely to slow the fall. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro continues to fall and the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  continues to dominate, the Australian dollar will continue \par \par \uc2  under pressure," said National Australia Bank strategist Greg \par \par \uc2  McKenna. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie traded as low as US$0.5407 offshore, down from \par \par \uc2  Monday's local closing level around $0.5425. \par \par \uc2       The Australian dollar has ignored positive fundamentals \par \par \uc2  all year, taking its cues instead from movements in the euro, \par \par \uc2  which continues to hit record lows. \par \par \uc2      "Policymakers may not like it, but the reality is that the \par \par \uc2  market, for the moment, is wedded to this link," said NAB's \par \par \uc2  McKenna. \par \par \uc2      This leaves any turnaround in the Aussie dependent on \par \par \uc2  coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rescue the euro, a \par \par \uc2  prospect which most analysts say is highly unlikely before the \par \par \uc2  U.S. presidential election in November. \par \par \uc2  As if sentiment surrounding the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't \par \par \uc2  bad enough, dealers also said new concerns over Asian markets \par \par \uc2  were providing another deadweight. \par \par \uc2  The Korean and Taiwanese stock markets were battered to \par \par \uc2  their lows for the year on Monday as investors responded to \par \par \uc2  rising oil prices, a weaker Wall Street and worries that \par \par \uc2  corporate reforms in the region are moving too slowly. \par \par \uc2  "There's a hint of distress in global markets at the \par \par \uc2  moment, although it's not clear whether it will develop into \par \par \uc2  something more dangerous," said ABN Amro strategist Gerard \par \par \uc2  Minack. \par \par \uc2      The Australian dollar is often traded as a proxy for less \par \par \uc2  liquid Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The RBA was widely suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several \par \par \uc2  occasions in the past week and is seen likely to enter the \par \par \uc2  market again should the Aussie threaten fibonacci support at \par \par \uc2  $0.5400. \par \par \uc2  But any action would merely slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  With net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of some A$10 billion, the \par \par \uc2  RBA does not have the firepower on its own to engineer a \par \par \uc2  turnaround. \par \par \uc2  While no-one is willing to call a bottom for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  some see signs of a potential turnaround in the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  from the new mood of pessimism on Wall Street as the weak euro \par \par \uc2  and rising oil prices carve into corporate earnings. \par \par \uc2  "I've cried wolf enough times before, so I don't want to \par \par \uc2  exaggerate the importance of these recent events," said ABN \par \par \uc2  Amro's Minack. \par \par \uc2  "However, what we are seeing makes a degree of sense - \par \par \uc2  equity markets are realising that growth is slowing and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength is pinching offshore profits." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9i07f60\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
