\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr To New Low Vs Dlr; Trades Under $0.5485 \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2000\par 17:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The Australian dollar fell to a new all-time low against its U.S. counterpart in New York trading, dropping below the previous record bottom of $0.5485 at around 11.30 a.m. EDT (1530 GMT). \par \par \uc2  At 11.40 a.m., the Australian dollar was changing hands at $0.5475, its lowest level so far. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar broke through its all-time low of $0.5585 late Friday morning York as dealers sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on weakness in the euro. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar's slide occurred as the euro dipped below $0.8600 after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceased buying euros as part of a widely publicized housekeeping \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 13:10 p.m. EDT (1710 GMT) the euro remains above its all-time low of $0.8550 at $0.8593. The Australian dollar is trading at $0.5463, after dippinmg as far as $0.5446. \par \par \uc2  Both the euro and the Australian dollar have declined sharply against the U.S. dollar in recent weeks with analysts blaming the continued draw of the strong U.S. economy for the slide. \par \par \uc2  Economic growth in both Europe and Australia has been strong but has lagged behind that seen in the U.S. this year. \par \par \uc2  "There has been a strong correlation between the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  driven by foreign investors piling into dollars," said Andrew Chaveriat, technical analyst at BNP Paribas in New York. \par \par \uc2  In the last six months there has been a 84% correlation between moves in the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and in the last three months there has been a 90% correlation. \par \par \uc2  There is no sign of the trend reversing and the Australian dollar could hit 52 cents in the coming weeks, Chaveriat said. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar's decline has taken many analysts by surprise, however, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to receive a boost from the Olympic Games in Australia. Chase Securities estimated that the event would generate A$3 billion in tourist revenues. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reported to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  numerous time in the last couple of weeks to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reserve Bank of Australia official in New York said that no comments\par would be made on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par -By Christine Richard, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4384;\par  christine.richard@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010804dw9f00n1v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
