\par\par \b \uc2  A$ holds above record lows vs dollar,yen in Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2000\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar held ground around US$0.56 on Friday, pulling away from record lows touched a day earlier amid short-covering ahead of a key meeting of European finance ministers this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar had matched its US$0.5530 record low set in August 1998 and hit record lows against the yen on Thursday despite dealers saying the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the break of US$0.56 in European trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro's recovery from its own record lows against the dollar late on Thursday gave respite to the battered Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As the Australian dollar has been moving in sync with the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lately, its near-term outlook seems to be linked or whether or not European ministers will issue a euro-supportive statement at their meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible renewed and more aggressive RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also keeping the Australian dollar propped, they added. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of short-covering going in the Aussie and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs ahead of the Ecofin meeting," said a dealer at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "In addition, there are still lingering fears of possible RBA action after the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  By 0930 GMT, the Australian dollar was hovering around US$0.5595 , up more than one third of a cent on the day. \par \par \uc2  Analysts doubted however any RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have long-lasting effects on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were relatively small. \par \par \uc2  "The Australian dollar has been quiet overnight, with no evidence of further RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Deutsche Bank in a client note. \par \par \uc2  "Still, the outlook for the Aussie remains weak, especially since the RBA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  firepower is actually quite limited with net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of only some US$6.7 billion." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the New Zealand dollar was struggling below US$0.42 , still within reach of this week's record lows around US$0.4130 it set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen said on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undervalued and oversold, bringing minor relief to the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at three-day peaks around C$1.4775 against the U.S. dollar ahead of Canadian jobs data for August at 1100 GMT and second quarter capacity untilisation at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9808gkz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
