\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2 's RBA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again To Calm Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2  By Clyde Russell and Iain McDonald \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 08:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY -(Dow Jones)- The Australian dollar stumbled to another two-year low Thursday, prompting a second day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Reserve Bank of Australia stepped in briefly around midday to calm a disorderly market as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped to an intraday low of US$0.5595, a level not seen since August 1998. \par \par \uc2  That slide, in a scaled-down version of Wednesday's activity, was again in part triggered by a slump in the euro to a fresh record low of US$0.8637. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, along with a faster-than-expected recovery in the euro, pushed the Australian dollar to as high as US$0.5643. It settled at US$0.5642 in late trading, still shy of the US$0.5662 local close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank is clearly in the market," said a senior dealer at an Australian bank. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer at one of the four major local banks said: "It was discussed in the market that the Reserve Bank had been in." The major banks are usually used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct its onmarket orders. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers were adamant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second day, citing the modest recovery in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the rumored activity. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday was said to have dealt widely through brokers although in only small amounts after the Australian dollar hit a low of US$0.5613. The buying yesterday prompted a very sharp turnaround in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to US$0.5670. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's buying seems more likely to have been done more discretely and directly through a very small number of commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  Sustained weakness in the euro led to the Australian dollar falling again Thursday, taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the psychological US$0.5600 level and within distance of its all-time low of US$0.5530 hit on August 27, 1998, when the Asian financial crisis was at its peak. \par \par \uc2  That record low led to the last major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank, spending upwards of A$3 billion. The scale of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time around is said not be anywhere near as large. \par \par \uc2  Dealers believe it spend between A$50 million and A$100 million Wednesday's, and probably less Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants remain nervous and dealers expect volatile trading sessions ahead, especially if the euro keeps plumbing record lows. Although, as one trader at an Australian bank put it, "the market has got a little bit more used" to these nervous trading conditions. \par \par \uc2  "I expect very volatile trading for the next 12-24 hours rather than a new range," said Paul Macarounas, Rothschild Australia treasury manager. He said the local unit could rally up to US$0.5650 on a short squeeze, especially if the euro stabilizes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Aussie Victim Of U.S. Dollar Strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Geoff Bowmer, divisional director at Macquarie Bank, said the\par Australian dollar is still a victim of U.S. dollar strength,\par particularly against the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think you can separate the Aussie from the euro," Bowmer\par said, adding the euro "still has a little way to go" before bottoming.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bowmer believes despite the reports of Reserve Bank action in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the local unit may yet drop below its all-time\par low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National Australia Bank market strategist Greg McKenna said the U.S.\par dollar "remains omnipotent".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "(Wednesday's) price action will make sellers wary of selling near\par areas of 'official interest' but it is hardly going to draw in long-term\par capital," McKenna said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the Australian dollar remains a sell on rallies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But in the medium term, there may be sufficient good news for the\par Australian dollar to convince investors that it is a good bet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Second quarter gross domestic product data are due Wednesday with\par preliminary expectations for annual growth to accelerate to around 5.0%\par from 4.3% in the first quarter, which could encourage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to hike rates early next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The first quarter numbers sparked a rally in the Australian dollar in\par June, taking the unit back above US$0.6000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, good economic numbers may not be enough as Thursday's\par employment data indicated. The market had expected a drop of 10,000\par jobs, but instead got a gain 0f 24,100 in August. The Australian dollar\par did rally a touch on the news before a fall in the euro sent it the\par other way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Clyde Russell, Dow Jones Newswires, 612 8235-2958\par clyde.russell@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9704c2c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
