\par\par \b \uc2  Macfarlane says  \highlight22\uc2 forex operations \highlight\uc2  not  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 110 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2000\par 04:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, May 22 (Reuters) - Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ian Macfarlane said on Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not a form of indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In recent months, the Reserve Bank has been meeting the government's routine foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs from its own reserves. \par \par \uc2  "We've been choosing not to replenish our reserves in the market," Macfarlane said in response to a question from a parliamentary committee. \par \par \uc2  "We don't call that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some people might quibble about that, but that is about semantics." \par \par \uc2  (Melbourne newsroom, 613-9286-1435, melbourne.newsroom@reuters.com). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5m004dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
