\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dollar Down Late; Bonds Lower On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Woes \b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2000\par 09:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY -(Dow Jones)- The Australian dollar is lower late Friday, having taken on a weak tone in the wake of its slide below the key US$0.6000 level overnight and during Australian trading hours, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bond market is also weaker, having been dragged down by the lackluster performance of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0651 GMT, the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at US$0.5991, down from US$0.6045 late Thursday in Sydney. The local unit was also quoted at Y62.90, down from Y63.41 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded steadily lower since the end of Australasian trading Thursday and dealers don't expect it to stop in the medium- to long-term. But there is a possibility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could squeeze up if it finds support at US$0.5970-80 in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  "I think we could go lower - the trend is your friend after all," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Citibank. "But I think people will start to get worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The market was spooked overnight when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped below 60 U.S. cents and then spiked up sharply, with dealers saying there were rumors the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said they haven't observed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank, but added that it's not impossible that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in the market buying small parcels of the Australian dollar in order to take the steam out of its falls. \par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds at its support, then dealers say it could retrace back up to US$0.6030-40. But dealers suggest that it's unlikely to break above US$0.6070-80 - a level that's seen good offers in recent days. \par \par \uc2  "We need a circuit-breaker to turn this trend around," said John Basile, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  marketing manager at Colonial State Bank. \par \par \uc2  That circuit-breaker could come in the form of U.S. non-farm payrolls data for March coming in outside economists' expectations, given that some observers suggest there are several special factors that need to be accounted for during the month. \par \par \uc2  A strong payroll figure will put further pressure on the Federal Reserve to increase U.S. interest rates and depress the U.S. asset markets. Such an eventuality could well give the Australian dollar a small fillip, Basile said. \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones survey of economists, shows a consensus expectation for a rise of 400,000 in the number of people on the payroll. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While Australian bonds have been depressed by the poor performance of\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they haven't been given a positive lead by the U.S.\par Treasurys market either. That market has been weakened as participants\par have taken profits ahead of a potential stock market rally at the start\par of U.S. trading.\par    10.0% Oct. bond '02:   6.29% vs.  6.31%\par    7.50% Sep. bond '09:   6.28% vs.  6.27%\par    SFE Jun 3Y Futures:   93.59  dn   0.06\par    SFE Jun 10Y Futures:  93.660 dn   0.060