\par\par \b \uc2  Australian dollar weakens back towards US$0.60. \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 6 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar eased in Europe on Thursday, eyeing the 18-month lows set against the U.S. dollar earlier this week as the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's concern about its weakness dampened the impact of its rate hike. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of Australia raised the official cash rate by 25 basis points to 5.75 percent on Wednesday, expressing concern in its accompanying statement about the weakness of the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The RBA statement is still a focus," said Tony Beard, senior institutional sales manager at National Australia Bank in London. "It has taken some of the gloss off the 25 basis point hike, but we are stuck in a US$0.6010/50 range for the moment." \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar failed to garner too much support from data on Thursday showing Australian employment rose a moderate 8,300 in March, building on the near 60,000 jump in February. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said two large sell orders in European trade pushed the Australian dollar\tab   down to US$0.6020 by 0930 GMT, its lowest level since Tuesday, but added that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was strongly supported at these levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts dismissed speculation made in recent weeks that the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the foreign exchanges to defend the Australian dollar below US$0.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We would not expect the RBA to aggressively try and influence the exchange rate - this is not their style," ABN AMRO London-based analysts said in a client note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Australian dollar has some way to go before the all clear can be sounded, US$0.62 to be precise," they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Zealand dollar\tab   held above US$0.50, in the middle of recent ranges, but strengthened to seven-month highs in Europe against the ailing Australian dollar\tab      at NZ$1.2018.\par The Canadian dollar\tab   held to the centre of recent ranges around 1.45 to the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen speaks at 1500 GMT, but analysts said he was not expected to resolve the ongoing debate on whether Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will match further U.S. interest rate hikes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Carolyn Cohn, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4602vbr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
