\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dollar Dips To 18-Month Low; Bonds Softer \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2000\par 00:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY -(Dow Jones)- The Australian dollar is weaker early Friday but is above the US$0.6000 level it dipped below late Thursday in New York, while bond prices fell in sympathy with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The local dollar hit an 18-month low of US$0.5992 as market participants realized the long-awaited challenge to the psychological US$0.6000 barrier. \par \par \uc2  At 2230 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at US$0.6012, down from US$0.6045 late Thursday in Sydney. The local unit was also at Y63.02, down from Y63.41 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at an Australian bank said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped on selling by a European investment bank, and when the U.S. banks also started selling, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't hold at US$0.6000. \par \par \uc2  "There were a lot of stops triggered under US$0.6000...but it recovered quickly," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said there were rumors of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London, "but nothing has been substantiated." \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said he has seen no evidence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying the local unit and he expects the Australian dollar to consolidate around US$0.6020 now that stops have been taken out. \par \par \uc2  Prices for Australian government bonds and bond futures contracts are also weaker, weighed down by the persistent weakness in the local dollar and the perception that this will encourage the Reserve Bank to tighten interest rates again. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasurys fell Thursday on a stronger performance from U.S. equities and this is also leading local bonds lower. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10.0% Oct. bond '02:   6.32% vs.  6.31%\par    7.50% Sep. bond '09:   6.30% vs.  6.27%\par    SFE Jun 3Y Futures:   93.60  dn   0.05\par    SFE Jun 10Y Futures:  93.690 dn   0.035\par    3-10 Yr Yield Spread  -0.02  vs. -0.04\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S.:  0.38  vs.  0.38\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Clyde Russell; 612-8235-2958\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1054 22765 4109 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4601t3j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
