\par\par \b \uc2  RBA says bought A$ options in Aug 98  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) purchased call options on the Australian dollar as a means of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last August when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at record lows, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its annual report released on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The options had since been resold at a profit, the RBA said in its 1998/99 (July-June) annual report tabled in parliament. \par \par \uc2  The RBA said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1998/99 all occurred in late August and early September 1998, and amounted to A$665 million including the options. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June of 1998, when speculative selling of the Australian dollar started on a large scale, amounted to A$2.6 billion, the RBA said. \par \par \uc2  The 1998/99 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August and September came as the Australian dollar fell to a record low of $0.5530 in late August. \par \par \uc2  "Instead of simply relying on outright purchases of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it had done in the past, the bank also purchased call options on the Australian dollar - that is the right to buy Australian dollars at a predetermined price," the RBA said. \par \par \uc2  The RBA said the options purchase allowed it to generate significant market demand for the Aussie, initially through the hedging activities of the dealers who had sold the options. \par \par \uc2  "In the event, the overshooting of the exchange rate was quickly reversed, and the bank resold the options (which were by then in profit) once it judged the danger period had passed," the annual report said. \par \par \uc2  The RBA said the use of options increased its flexibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the purchase of the call options involved very low risk, as there was no obligation to exercise the option but if it did, the overall effect on its assets would be the same as if it had purchased the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Since April, the Bank has sold A$1.507 billion Australian dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it rebuilds the reserves run down buying the Australian dollar in 1997/98 and 1998/99. \par \par \uc2  ((John Mair, Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800, john.mair@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8v01dbm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
