\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk June A$ Sales Not Seen As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 12:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Australian dollar sales in June by the Reserve Bank of Australia weren't part of a plan to cap the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but rather part of its usual procedure of covering its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions with the government. \par \par \uc2  Westpac Banking Corp. senior economist Helen Camp said Wednesday that the Australian-dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second quarter "reflect the fact that the Reserve Bank has returned to normal practice in its handling of Government \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements." \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank said in its semiannual statement in May that "in light of the greater stability in the market and the higher average level of the exchange rate, the Bank in mid-April resumed its normal practice of covering the Government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs by purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market." \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  met the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs by running down its own reserves so as not to aggravate an already weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It resumed in April the procedure of covering the government's needs through market transactions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had recovered from an all-time low of US$0.5525 in August 1998. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at US$0.6455. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1059GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7l05dsj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
