\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Central Bk -2: Last  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In Sept \b0\par\par\uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 1999\par 08:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't buy or sell Australian dollars in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market transactions in March, according to figures issued Monday. \par \par \uc2  The data, included in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin, reflect \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions against the Australian dollar undertaken by the Reserve Bank with authorized \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Australia or banks overseas. But the figures don't account for any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap transactions the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have completed or any transactions it undertook on behalf of the government. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last bought Australian dollars in August and September 1998, when it purchased A$310 million and A$355 million, respectively. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an all-time low of US$0.5525 in August. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0653GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4j02x6d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
