\par\par \b \uc2  Panel Says Australia's Monetary Policy Helped 1998 Economy \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 08:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CANBERRA -(Dow Jones)- Australia's strong economic performance over the past year relative to others in the region is due in part to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's approach to monetary policy and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said David Hawker, chairman of the federal Parliament's economics committee. \par \par \uc2  In a speech to Parliament on Monday, Hawker - a member of the ruling Liberal-National coalition - said the economy has fared much better during the recent financial crisis than many other countries in Asia and the Pacific. \par \par \uc2  The economy grew 4.7% in 1998, while the consumer price index rose 1.6% over the year. \par \par \uc2  Hawker earlier in the day tabled a committee report on the RBA's performance, which centered on an appearance by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ian Macfarlane before the panel in December. \par \par \uc2  "While unemployment is still too high, 7.5% in January, and the most recent data put the current account deficit at 5% of gross domestic product in the last four quarters, the economy has still done very well," Hawker said. \par \par \uc2  "This is in part attributable to the astute performance of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the exchange rate," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets a number of times in 1998 to support the Australian dollar, a freely floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it slid to an all-time low of US$0.5530 in August. \par \par \uc2  "The bank's steady, deliberative approach to monetary policy has paid off," the economics committee chairman said. \par \par \uc2  "However, this good performance should not lead to complacency as the impact of the crisis is far from over." \par \par \uc2  The RBA cut its overnight cash rate just once in 1998, lowering it to 4.75% on Dec. 2 from 5%. \par \par \uc2  In the report, the committee and the RBA backed a more detailed analysis of the impact of hedge funds on local financial market participants. \par \par \uc2  "Hedge funds are of great concern to national and international financial regulators and governments. Hedge funds have generated a new source of financial instability in the world economy," Hawker said. \par \par \uc2  "While hedge funds are mainly U.S., work by (regulators) has revealed Australian banks also have exposure through lending, and as the counterparty to a swap transaction, particularly a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap transaction." \par \par \uc2  According to the report, the committee together with the RBA and many other groups, supports three lines of action on hedge funds: finding out how large the hedge funds are, both on and off balance sheet; banks reviewing their relationships with hedge funds, which in some cases appear to have become quite incestuous; and bringing hedge funds into the disclosure net and possibly the supervision net. \par \par \uc2  The committee also backed a study of changes in commercial bank's retail fees over the past 20 years, which it says is a "critical concern" to the community. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 612-6208-0901; \par \par \uc2  ben.pedley@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv38021b1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
