\par\par \b \uc2  RBA says A$  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  not meant as line in sand. \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1998\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Sept 1 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) said its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had limited aims and it had been careful to avoid drawing a line in the sand at particular levels. \par \par \uc2  In its annual report, the bank said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be useful in restoring a sense of two-way risk and lessening the momentum which might otherwise result in overshooting. \par \par \uc2  "The aim has been a modest one: to limit the size of movements once a substantial adjustment has already occurred i.e. to trim the peaks and troughs," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank believes that in the long run it is the effective \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of monetary policy which determines the level of the exchange rate, and that it would be futile in the absence of sound monetary policy to use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pursue a particular level for the exchange rate," the RBA said. \par \par \uc2  With this in mind the bank acted in June to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restore some stability to the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It (the RBA) bought a considerable amount of Australian dollars at levels between 62 U.S. cents and 60 U.S. cents, though taking care to avoid drawing "lines in the sand"," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The RBA said it had accepted that a significant depreciation in the Australian dollar in 1997/98 was appropriate as a response to the Asian crisis. \par \par \uc2  In June, however, speculative selling by large international funds managers was clearly evident and natural buyers of the dollar, such as exporters, whose transactions were normally linked to trade flows, began to trade speculatively, it said. \par \par \uc2  "Judging a potential for further instability, and recognising that there had already been a large adjustment in the exchange rate, the Bank felt that there was a case for it to be on the other side of the market," the RBA said. \par \par \uc2  The June \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did briefly help the A$ stabilise, but since mid-July it has tumbled again to reach a record low of $0.5530 last week. The RBA was rumoured to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  under 56 cents late last week, but has so far refused to comment. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank remains strongly of the view that the floating exchange rate regime has served Australia very well over the 15 years since its introduction," the RBA added. \par \par \uc2  The bank also emphasised that when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  it was not "spending" money, as sometimes described by the media, but exchanging one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  asset for another. \par \par \uc2  "Because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank through-out the post-float period has followed the pattern of of buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is cheap and selling when it is expensive, it has yielded significant profits," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June continued this pattern since the bank was selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought in late 1996 or early 1997 when the A$ was much stronger. \par \par \uc2  "As such, in contrast to some popular claims that, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank was handing easy profits to speculators, it was in fact realising substantial profits on earlier purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the bank said. \par \par \uc2  Some of these profits were reflected in the A$2.7 billion of 1997/98 earnings paid to the Commonwealth government. "And some will be reflected in the coming year when the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was sold is delivered," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar stood at 57.05 U.S. cents on Tuesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  ((Sydney newsroom, 61-2 9373 1800)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du9101w30\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
