\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Dn Midmorning After Reaching Lows Overnight \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 01:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is hovering tentatively in lower levels midmorning Friday, although is off its new post-float low reached overnight. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid to US$0.5525, its lowest level reached since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1983. \par \par \uc2  An escalation of the turmoil in Russian markets reverberated throughout global markets overnight, with commodity-based economies like Australia coming under renewed pressure, according to dealers. Russia's problems were accentuated by unconfirmed rumors president Boris Yeltsin might resign, dealers added. The KR-CRB index of commodity prices declined a further 1.88 points overnight to 196.24 overnight, while gold was last quoted at US$276.55/oz, below US$281.05/oz late in Sydney Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar bounced off its lows overnight, however, on talk that the U.S. federal reserve sold around US$100 million for Australian dollar's on behalf of the Reserve Bank of Australia near the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lows. Both the U.S. federal reserve or \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 2340 GMT, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted at US$0.5585, below US$0.5647 late in Sydney Thursday. It also is at Y79.12, below Y81.12 Thursday, while the trade-weighted index has fallen to 52.5 from 53.1. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say market participants are on watch for signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar Friday. Meanwhile, events offshore are likely to overshadow the release of domestic second-quarter current-account and net foreign debt figures at 0130 GMT Friday. \par \par \uc2  A domestic bank analyst suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might see some consolidation of recent losses Friday. She sees the Australian dollar trading in a US$0.5530-US$0.5610 intra day band. \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer warns that further commodity price weakness likely will see traders test the Reserve Bank of Australia's resolve. He noted, however, that technical charts show the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly in oversold territory. \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2354GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07cf1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
