\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dollar/12-Yr Low -2: U.S. Sellers Noted \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 04:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is weaker at midday Wednesday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  having extended recent losses to reach a new 12-year low. \par \par \uc2  U.S. sellers and selling on the International Monetary Market have been noted Wednesday, according to one domestic bank dealer, driving the Australian dollar down through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight low at US$0.5738 to touch US$0.5730 around midday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lowest level reached since July 1986. \par \par \uc2  Weighing on the Australian dollar is turmoil in Russia and emerging markets, which is notably bearish for commodity prices, according to dealers. Other factors not helping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are a weaker yen Wednesday, and political uncertainty stemming from market speculation that the federal government might call an election by this weekend, the election to be held in October. The next federal election must be held by May 1999. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar "looks heavy, it feels heavy", the domestic bank dealer says. He adds, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to find some support earlier in the local morning from traders caught holding short positions versus the yen, and from a few local buyers. \par \par \uc2  There has been no talk of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the Australian dollar Wednesday. The dealer doesn't anticipate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whilst trading remains "orderly". \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted at US$0.5735, down from US$0.5801 late in Sydney Tuesday. It also is at Y83.05, below Y83.79 Tuesday, while the trade-weighted index has fallen to 54.3 from 54.7 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the next key level to watch on the downside is the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's post-float low of US$0.5717 reached in July 1986. \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0242GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8q0796y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
