\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/Post-Float Low -2:Follows Overnight Tumble \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 01:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones Australia and New Zealand Report \par \uc2 DJAN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar has slid further in morning dealings Thursday to a new post-1983-float trough of US$0.5605. \par \par \uc2  This followed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide to US$0.5623 overnight as the Russian ruble fell, prompting further weakness in emerging markets and commodity prices, according to dealers. The KR-CRB index of commodity prices closed down 1.65 pts at 198.12 overnight. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar has since edged off its lows, and at 2325 GMT is quoted at US$0.5633, down from US$0.5735 late in Sydney Wednesday. It also is at Y81.10, below Y82.90 Wednesday, while the trade-weighted index has slipped to 53.4 from 54.3. \par \par \uc2  While dealers have reported no sight of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar, the central banks of Canada, Denmark, Greece, Turkey, Hungary and Venezuela were forced to defend their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Growing fears of global economic recession", sparked by the spread of Asian economic turmoil to Russia and emerging markets, continues to weigh on the Australian dollar, according to one senior domestic bank dealer. Consequently, "the momentum is to the downside" with US$0.5500 now the key psychological target, he adds. \par \par \uc2  At these levels, traders are on watch for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dealer says. However, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "might be a little concerned at the speed of the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) move" lower overnight, the decline has generally been "orderly" and "hasn't been purely speculative", the dealer comments, as was the case in June when the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar during its yen-led slide to US$0.5800. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2335GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djan000020010916du8q003iy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
