\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -3: Global Mkts,Commodities Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 09:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  David Bassanesse, senior economist at Australia and New Zealand Banking Group, agreed that it was "possible" the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it continued to fall. \par \par \uc2  Concern about the threat of turmoil in Asia and Russia spreading to emerging markets, and lower commodity prices could see "hedge funds look at the Australian dollar intensively," Bassanese said. \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while it is falling hasn't always been successful, Bassanese said, noting that such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is often aptly described as "leaning into the wind." Consequently, he suggested that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  might "look to (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) when the Australian dollar is headed up rather than down" to reinforce any strength. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  commented in its August bulletin that while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June "acted as a counterweight to the hedge funds and restored a normal two-way flow of business...on balance, the exchange rate continued to fall." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that the Australian dollar bottomed once the U.S. Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, prompting a stronger Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which in turn supported the Australian dollar's recovery. \par \par \uc2  On an approach to the Australian dollar's post-float low of US$0.5717, Westpac's Camp anticipates "the market likely would slow itself up," regardless of whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Even if the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to step into the market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "won't take on the market in a big way", Camp said, although "there would be no harm in the Reserve Bank of Australia showing its presence if (the fall) becomes disorderly." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0714GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8o076up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
