\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Weaker Late, After Touching 12-Year Low \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 08:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar was weaker late Monday, although off session lows reached as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to its lowest level in twelve years. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar broke under its previous 1998 low of US$0.5800 to reach US$0.5782 Monday, its lowest level touched since July 1986. Dealers said there was no sign of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June during the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-led slide to US$0.5800. \par \par \uc2  The main factors weighing on the Australian dollar include the threat of the turmoil in Asia and Russia spreading to the emerging markets, according to dealers. This is bearish for global growth and commodity prices. Market participants also remain concerned about the state of the Japanese economy, including the country's troubled financial sector, they added. \par \par \uc2  At 0630 GMT, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was changing hands at US$0.5811, down from US$0.5875 late in Sydney Friday. It also was at Y84.11, above Y83.92 Friday, while the trade-weighted index fell to 55.0 from 55.3. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar continued to keep a close eye on U.S. dollar-yen dealings Monday, commented Matt Gilmour, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bankers Trust Australia Ltd. He noted that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide to US$0.5782 mid-morning coincided with a dip in the yen versus the U.S. dollar. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's subsequent climb off its session lows then helped support the Australian dollar's recovery to a US$0.5825 peak during the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  There was little on the domestic front to provide direction Monday. Indeed, there is little on the local economic calendar until the release of a spate of second-quarter economic figures later in the week. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, attention is expected to remain focused on activity in offshore markets, notably Japan, Russia and the emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0647GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8o076rh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
