\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Wary Of Hedge Fund Players \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 08:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar in June when it spent A$2.60 billion in an attempt to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-led slide to US$0.5800. \par \par \uc2  The yen is still playing a part in the Australian dollar's weakness, with the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also suffering from concern about the health of the Japanese economy, including problems in the country's banking sector. Japan is Australia's largest trading partner. \par \par \uc2  Given the problems in offshore markets, it's not surprising to see the Australian dollar under pressure, Camp said. She added that the threat of further deterioration in such markets could drive the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still lower. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank of Australia is concerned about the Australian dollar and is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," commented John Edwards, chief economist at HSBC Markets. \par \par \uc2  "Beyond a certain point, the gain in competitiveness (from a lower \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is outweighed by the contribution to higher inflation, and also by the risk that a falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  engenders concern about the quality of Australian credit," commented Edwards. \par \par \uc2  In considering the likelihood of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Edwards pointed to comments made by the Reserve Bank of Australia in its August bulletin, in which the Bank cited two factors that had supported its decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. \par \par \uc2  Firstly, "participants in the market (had begun) to believe that the Australian authorities were happy to see the dollar continue to fall," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  However, Edwards remarked that the fact that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't happy with the decline. \par \par \uc2  Secondly, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that "hedge funds (had) stepped up their profile in the market." This resulted in a drop in liquidity, as market participants became reluctant to trade while speculators took command of the market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0645GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8o076rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
