\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Under US$0.5800 -2:Offshore Mkt Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 02:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones Australia and New Zealand Report \par \uc2 DJAN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar has dipped under US$0.5800 in morning dealings Monday, the move taking the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its 1998 low to levels not seen in twelve years. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar has slid to a low so far of US$0.5782, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure from a number of factors, according to one domestic bank dealer. These include concern about the state of the Japanese economy, especially the banking sector, and the spread of turmoil in Asia and Russia to the emerging economies. In particular, he says the latter has negative implications for commodity prices. \par \par \uc2  Under the weight of the above concerns, traders are seen paring back their long positions, according to the dealer, which is fueling the Australian dollar's slide. However, he says that there has been reasonable two-way interest Monday, and describes trading as "orderly". \par \par \uc2  The dealer adds that there has been no talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-June, when the Australian dollar touched a US$0.5800 low. \par \par \uc2  At 0010 GMT, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted at US$0.5785, down from US$0.5875 late in Sydney Friday. It also is at Y84.05, above Y83.92 Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the Australian dollar remains under US$0.5810, risk remains\par weighted to the downside, the dealer comments. He adds that the next key\par level to watch on the downside is the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's post-float low of\par US$0.5717 touched in July 1986.\par    -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0023GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djan000020010916du8o003g0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
