\par\par \b \uc2  INSIGHT-Australian debt retreat on wary A$. \b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 00:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FUTURES     *SUP-RES\tab  *2ND SUP-RES   *3RD SUP-RES   *RSI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  10-YEAR(SEP)*94.280-94.440 *94.280-94.470 *94.180-94.520 *35.17 \par \par \uc2  3-YEAR (SEP)*94.55-94.65   *94.47-94.72   *94.36-94.78   *46.43 \par \par \uc2  90-DAY (SEP)*94.50-94.57   *94.47-94.62   *94.41-94.68   *45.32 \par \par \uc2  -----------------------(June 19)------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      *Australian debt futures stayed in retreat from Thursday's \par \par \uc2  early dayside peaks during SYCOM trade with the short end \par \par \uc2  looking to test their post-USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakout levels. \par \par \uc2      *Fitch-IBCA places \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on negative watch. \par \par \uc2      *U.S. Treasuries end cautiously firm on partial US$ rebound. \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, June 19 (Reuters) - Australian debt futures stayed in retreat from Thursday's early dayside peaks during SYCOM trade with short end contracts looking to test their post-USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakout levels. \par \par \uc2  September three-year bond futures ended five basis points lower at 94.59, slipping back from yesterday's 94.72 high and close to the 94.55/94.57 level seen prior to the surge in the local dollar to 62.00 U.S. cents. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since rowed back to around 60.80 cents in tandem with a back-tracking yen awaiting Japanese policy developments to back up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  September bills shed seven basis points by 94.52 at the end of SYCOM, easing through perceived support at 94.57 and now risking a further retreat to 94.35/94.37. \par \par \uc2  Analysts such has been the wild fluctuations in recent weeks on the sharp turnaround in policy sentiment that support/resistance levels are now fairly well spaced out. \par \par \uc2  Ten-year bond futures also softened, ending after hours trade at 94.315 compared with Thursday's 94.370 pit close, but held support at 94.280. This saw the bond yield reverse its recent outperformance of the U.S. Treasuries, were yields ended cautiously lower on a partial recovery in the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Fitch-IBCA rating agency has put Australia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  AA long term debt rating on negative watch, but kept its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on AAA. \par \par \uc2  The agency said in view of the deteriorating regional economic environment, the country's AA rating sits uneasily with its high external debt levels. \par \par \uc2  ((Colin Brinsden, 61-2 9373-1800, \par \par \uc2  sydney.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02k7j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
